/**

@page swift_initial_conditions Initial conditions

There are two main ways to implement initial conditions for the
simulations:

  - Insert particle by coordinates (```InsertParticlesByCoordinates.py```).
  - Insert particles from an HDF5 file (```InsertParticlesFromHDF5File.py```).

The former option is typically complemented by an initialisation snippet that
sets the individual particle attributes (other than positions).
The latter option automatically sets (at least a subset of) the particle
attributes.

## Insert particle by coordinates.




A set of snippets for SPH benchmarks can be found at






## Insert particles from an HDF5 file.

A basic HDF5 reader that is compatible with IC files from the original Swift code is
implemented in ```InsertParticlesFromHDF5File.py```.
In order to make use of the HDF5 reader, Peano must have been configured with

          ./configure ... --enable-particles --enable-swift --with-hdf5

Since this also has to be supported by the compiler used at the application
level, it is recommended to include the following flags:

          ./configure ...  --enable-particles --enable-swift --with-hdf5 \
                CXXFLAGS="-I/$HDF5_ROOT/include" \
                LDFLAGS="-L/$HDF5_ROOT/lib" \
                LIBS="-lhdf5_hl_cpp -lhdf5_cpp -lhdf5_hl -lhdf5 -lstdc++"

where ``$HDF5_ROOT`` should be the directory that contains your local HDF5 installation,
e.g. ``/usr`` or ``/usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/hdf5/serial/``.








*/
